: verify by grep which files actually carry the '[operator-attested]' evidence contract (it is src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md, not plan_review_F1/E2/E6.md or a nonexistent coach_moves.py 'move 14'), and update AC-6's diff-guard file list accordingly — or drop the claim that these four files carry the contract.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'they are shipped reviewer prompts at src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_F1.md, plan_review_E2.md and plan_review_E6.md, with a fourth contract-text site at src/rebar/llm/plan_review/coach_moves.py (coach move 14)'","Grep `attest`/`vote outcome`/`outside the codebase` in plan_review_F1.md, plan_review_E2.md, plan_review_E6.md → no matches (only unrelated coaching lines)","coach_moves.py lines 1-40: MOVE_REGISTRY keys are '1','2','3' and the docstring states 'moves 1-9,11,12'; no move 14, no attestation/contract text (grep `attested`/`vote`/`change id`/`14` → no matches)","completion_verifier.md:39-94 carries the actual contract: 'attestation: a statement in the ticket that reports a checkable fact about the outside world (a change/deploy id, a vote result, an observed log line or console value, a timestamp)' and the concrete-vs-vague bar","docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md: grep `operator-attested` → no matches, contradicting the 'GENERATED from the registry' contract-site claim"],"finding":"The plan's load-bearing claim about WHERE the '[operator-attested]' contract text lives is refuted by Grep/Read. Scope states the three 'OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE' statements 'are shipped reviewer prompts at src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_F1.md, plan_review_E2.md and plan_review_E6.md, with a fourth contract-text site at src/rebar/llm/plan_review/coach_moves.py (coach move 14)'. None of those four files carries the contract: grep for `attest`/`vote outcome`/`outside the codebase`/`change id` returns no matches in the three plan_review_*.md files, and coach_moves.py is a generic move catalog whose docstring enumerates 'moves 1-9,11,12' (no move 14, no contract text). The contract text the plan quotes ('a change id / vote outcome / timestamp', evidence that 'lives outside the codebase and is a concrete attestation recorded on the ticket') actually lives in src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md (lines 39-94). Additionally the plan claims docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md is 'GENERATED from the registry' and carries the contract, but that file contains no 'operator-attested' text at all.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fae97efe78eb0da2b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → 'Explicitly OUT of scope — the shipped contract text is NOT edited'; and AC-6","norm_id":"n13272b5e1031eff7","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":["Implementer sets up AC-6's `git diff --exit-code` over the four named files; it passes trivially because none of them carry the contract, giving false assurance of 'no cross-client behaviour change' while the real contract site (completion_verifier.md) is unguarded and could be edited without tripping the check.","A reader trusts 'coach move 14' as a fourth contract site and tries to preserve it byte-for-byte; there is no such move, so the safeguard is vacuous."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Replace the four named sites with the real one: add src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md to AC-6's `git diff --exit-code` list (and confirm whether docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md carries any contract text before listing it — grep shows it does not). Drop the 'coach move 14' claim, since coach_moves.py holds only generic moves 1-9,11,12.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_v